1
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:16,877
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:24,992
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:27,727
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:37,497
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:40,897
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you.

7
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:43,557
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, and so elusive.

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,737
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,837
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:55,697
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:58,000
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,597
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see.

15
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:08,877
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:11,000
Believe in wonder.

17
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:21,117
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,157
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,937
We'll live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,020 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,537
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:36,617
We don't want to live ordinary life.

24
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:39,777
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:42,460
We live in one another.

26
00:01:56,100 --> 00:01:57,982
I think you've got it backwards.

27
00:01:59,220 --> 00:02:00,700
The hiding thing, I mean.

28
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:08,960
Well, that is better.

29
00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:12,867
But it's a little late at this
point, And I can still see you.

30
00:02:13,260 --> 00:02:14,600
Shut up, lady!

31
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:17,957
Oh, and can you tell me
how your fever's doing?

32
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:18,870
It's choking!

33
00:02:27,540 --> 00:02:29,260
Keep it down, Chopper!

34
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:41,017
Your fever seems to have
gone down a little bit.

35
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:41,930
That's good.

36
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:44,160
You happy?

37
00:02:46,180 --> 00:02:47,010
Hmm.

38
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:50,400
Who are you?

39
00:02:51,860 --> 00:02:53,978
Yes, it's gone down several degrees.

40
00:02:54,080 --> 00:02:55,157
Should be all right.

41
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:58,417
I'm the only doctor
around here. Dr. Kureha.

42
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:00,900
But you can call me Dr. Rain, okay?

43
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:03,957
Oh, then that means we're on...

44
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:05,922
Looking for how I stay so young?

45
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:07,780
No, that's not it.

46
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:16,457
Anyway, yes, you're in the
castle on the mountain.

47
00:03:16,540 --> 00:03:19,757
In that case, there were two other people
who showed up here with me, weren't there?

48
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:22,193
Yeah, they're sleeping in the next room.

49
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:23,530
Very deeply.

50
00:03:23,613 --> 00:03:24,756
Two real tough guys.

51
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:30,500
This is what caused your sickness.

52
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:31,760
Wow, really?

53
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:35,109
You were bitten by a
bug called the kestia.

54
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:39,257
It's a poisonous tick that thrives in
jungles with high heat and humidity.

55
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:42,897
When it bites you, it introduces
a type of bacteria into your body.

56
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:46,627
These bacteria lay dormant for
five days, causing severe pain.

57
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:49,929
It causes a high fever,
a severe infection,

58
00:03:50,540 --> 00:03:52,952
myocarditis, and arteritis, not pleasant.

59
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:55,637
Given the infection's
progression in the affected area,

60
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:58,537
I'd guess you'd been infected
for about three days now.

61
00:03:58,620 --> 00:04:01,077
The pain you'd been feeling
must have been terrible,

62
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:04,857
but still it would have eased up in two
more days without any treatment at all.

63
00:04:04,940 --> 00:04:07,740
It would have gone away
in two days? Mm-hmm.

64
00:04:08,180 --> 00:04:12,062
You wouldn't be feeling any pain
whatsoever because you'd be dead.

65
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:16,437
This particular infection is
known as the five-day disease.

66
00:04:16,520 --> 00:04:19,617
I had heard that Kestia had died
out over a hundred years ago,

67
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:21,857
but I kept the antibiotic just in case.

68
00:04:21,940 --> 00:04:25,057
Where did you guys come from that
you may have been exposed to this?

69
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:29,140
Were you walking around some ancient
jungle with your belly showing?

70
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,080
No, ridiculous.

71
00:04:32,580 --> 00:04:33,410
Uh...

72
00:04:35,060 --> 00:04:37,317
Does this situation sound familiar at all?

73
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:39,282
What a crazy girl you are, then.

74
00:04:40,980 --> 00:04:42,460
Now, stay in bed.

75
00:04:42,660 --> 00:04:45,557
The treatment for the disease
isn't completely finished yet.

76
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:46,880
Thank you so much.

77
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:49,117
I'll be fine as long
as my fever goes down.

78
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:51,297
My body will take care
of itself after that.

79
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:53,177
Well, aren't you an optimistic one?

80
00:04:53,260 --> 00:04:55,137
This disease normally takes a course of

81
00:04:55,220 --> 00:04:57,317
treatment ten days long
to successfully cure.

82
00:04:57,400 --> 00:05:00,260
Even with medicines as
advanced as mine are,

83
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:01,877
your body will still
need at least three days?

84
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:03,136
to fully recuperate.

85
00:05:03,260 --> 00:05:08,025
If you don't want to risk more suffering
and possibly death, get some rest, girl.

86
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:09,700
I can't stay that long!

87
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:11,077
We need to get Vivi home!

88
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:12,160
Back to Alabasta!

89
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:19,367
When a patient leaves this castle, it's
because she's either cured or deceased.

90
00:05:19,700 --> 00:05:21,257
You aren't going anywhere, girl.

91
00:05:21,340 --> 00:05:22,869
You better get used to it.

92
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:52,887
He climbed this mountain
with his bare hands.

93
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:55,982
That's almost three miles
of sheer rock to go up.

94
00:05:57,620 --> 00:06:00,267
His entire body is on
the brink of frostbite.

95
00:06:00,420 --> 00:06:03,037
What was he thinking dressing
like that for such a climb?

96
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:04,937
Draw some hot water and throw him into it.

97
00:06:05,020 --> 00:06:06,897
This guy is bleeding a whole lot.

98
00:06:06,980 --> 00:06:09,780
He has six broken ribs
and a spinal fissure.

99
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:11,317
Can I operate on him, Dr.

100
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:12,230
E?

101
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:16,577
Apparently the most critical of
our three patients is this girl.

102
00:06:16,660 --> 00:06:17,660
This one's dying.

103
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:22,140
Chopper, have phenocall, cardiotonic,
and thiosaline ready for me.

104
00:06:22,320 --> 00:06:23,555
She has an infection?

105
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:27,652
Yes, and the infection isn't
from anywhere on this island.

106
00:06:33,820 --> 00:06:34,860
Don't worry, boy.

107
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:37,537
I'll make the bleeding kid
and the sick girl better.

108
00:06:37,620 --> 00:06:39,326
You can rest easy, all right?

109
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:43,060
Those two are my friends, okay?

110
00:06:49,140 --> 00:06:50,400
I figured that kid.

111
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:52,444
I'll save them, so don't worry.

112
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:54,404
Chopper, let's begin treatment.

113
00:06:58,480 --> 00:07:01,000
Those two are my f-friends, okay?

114
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:05,230
I'm hungry.

115
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:08,300
So hungry.

116
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:14,740
Need meat.

117
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:22,337
A renaissance stew should
be simmered in a large pot

118
00:07:22,420 --> 00:07:25,380
for three hours until all
the meat becomes tender.

119
00:07:28,400 --> 00:07:29,230
Venison.

120
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:41,760
Somebody help me!

121
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:51,557
Hold on, Luffy!

122
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:53,680
Let me cook this guy up first!

123
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:02,510
Nami!

124
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:03,770
Nami, dear!

125
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:05,457
You look like you're all better!

126
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:06,737
Getting there, thanks.

127
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:07,650
Right.

128
00:08:07,733 --> 00:08:09,851
One tasty venison dish for Nami coming up!

129
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:14,840
Come back!

130
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:19,340
I'm impressed.

131
00:08:19,640 --> 00:08:21,677
Those guys are already up and moving.

132
00:08:21,760 --> 00:08:22,590
Yeah, they are.

133
00:08:22,673 --> 00:08:25,013
Can you tell me about this talking deer?

134
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:26,517
Figured you'd ask about him.

135
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:28,520
Don't run away, meat!

136
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:29,760
Don't eat it yet!

137
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:36,520
Leave me alone!

138
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:37,976
His name is Chopper.

139
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:41,001
He's just a reindeer with
a blue nose, that's all.

140
00:08:41,780 --> 00:08:44,300
But normal reindeers don't talk.

141
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:49,277
If he's different from ordinary
reindeers in some way...

142
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:51,000
If he's different?

143
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:58,000
I am not food for you, okay?!

144
00:08:59,280 --> 00:09:02,957
If he's different, it's just because
he ate a human-human fruit, that's all.

145
00:09:03,040 --> 00:09:04,300
A human-human fruit.

146
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:05,960
A Devil Fruit, right?

147
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:08,710
That's right.

148
00:09:08,793 --> 00:09:11,717
He's still a reindeer, but now
he has the abilities of a human,

149
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:13,682
like talking and walking abroad.

150
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:16,100
No! This way!

151
00:09:16,900 --> 00:09:18,377
And also, he's a doctor.

152
00:09:18,460 --> 00:09:22,460
I taught Chopper everything that I
know about the field of medicine.

153
00:09:25,740 --> 00:09:26,760
What a shame.

154
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:27,900
Already over?

155
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:34,913
Well, that was disappointing, wasn't it?

156
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:41,590
Amazing.

157
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:43,530
Right!

158
00:09:43,613 --> 00:09:44,797
Zoro, that was a good job!

159
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:46,137
Just like I told you to do!

160
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:47,050
Yeah!

161
00:09:48,040 --> 00:09:48,870
Great.

162
00:09:48,953 --> 00:09:50,397
Now we can go over there
and look for Dalton.

163
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:51,310
Let's go!

164
00:09:53,780 --> 00:09:54,662
Thank you, sir.

165
00:09:57,260 --> 00:09:58,680
Hurry! Dig everywhere!

166
00:10:00,560 --> 00:10:01,817
So what's going on here?

167
00:10:01,900 --> 00:10:03,197
Why are they all so worked up?

168
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:04,717
I'll explain it all to you later.

169
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:06,857
For now, let's just give them a hand.

170
00:10:06,940 --> 00:10:07,960
Come on, Dalton.

171
00:10:08,280 --> 00:10:09,574
Please still be alive.

172
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:22,417
You should be one of
my crew please old lady

173
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:24,997
we really need to have a doctor on board.

174
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:27,817
Luffy you did tell me
that's your name isn't

175
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:30,117
that right yeah right
that's what i said old lady.

176
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:33,560
If i were you i'd be a little
more careful of what i say.

177
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:42,240
I'm still well within my youthful 130s
thank you jeez you're a tough old head.

178
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:47,162
Are you boys really asking
me to become a pirate?

179
00:10:47,680 --> 00:10:48,856
Don't be ridiculous.

180
00:10:49,040 --> 00:10:51,617
That would be an incredible
waste of my precious time.

181
00:10:51,700 --> 00:10:54,465
Besides, I have no interest
in life on the sea.

182
00:10:54,780 --> 00:10:56,400
Those are all lame excuses.

183
00:10:56,660 --> 00:10:58,337
It's about adventure, old woman.

184
00:10:58,420 --> 00:11:00,157
Well, this one's a slow learner.

185
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:02,887
Didn't I just tell you
to watch what you say?

186
00:11:03,140 --> 00:11:04,940
So these guys are pirates?

187
00:11:11,740 --> 00:11:14,440
Wait, food, come back here! Slow down!

188
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:17,920
Get back!

189
00:11:18,180 --> 00:11:19,945
That's enough of that, idiots!

190
00:11:27,340 --> 00:11:29,040
In just a few minutes,

191
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:32,277
I'm going to cook you a delicious
reindeer dish you'll never forget!

192
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:33,360
I don't think so!

193
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:38,117
I'll eat you guys first
before I let that happen!

194
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:39,060
Scary fact!

195
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:51,052
I don't care about food, I
just want some peace and quiet.

196
00:11:57,760 --> 00:11:58,590
Snow?

197
00:11:58,673 --> 00:12:00,933
But that shouldn't be inside the castle.

198
00:12:01,260 --> 00:12:02,200
It's freezing.

199
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:06,237
I'll close the door.

200
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:08,120
No, you need to stay in bed.

201
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:11,640
After all, you still have a fever.

202
00:12:12,380 --> 00:12:13,540
I don't think so.

203
00:12:13,740 --> 00:12:15,677
It seems like it's pretty much gone now.

204
00:12:15,760 --> 00:12:18,840
I lost him, at least for now. Dr.

205
00:12:18,940 --> 00:12:21,377
Ene's medicine works
quickly to reduce the fever.

206
00:12:21,460 --> 00:12:23,557
But the bacteria from
the castia will still

207
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:25,997
remain inside your body
for a little while longer.

208
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:29,021
So just take your antibiotic
shot and stay in bed.

209
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:32,100
Thank you. Hmm?

210
00:12:33,060 --> 00:12:36,354
You're the one who's been
taking care of me, aren't you?

211
00:12:38,080 --> 00:12:39,320
You just shut up!

212
00:12:39,660 --> 00:12:43,013
I don't need thanks from you
or any other low-life human!

213
00:12:44,660 --> 00:12:45,620
Don't mock me!

214
00:12:45,820 --> 00:12:48,291
Oh, never mind that, I'm just being silly.

215
00:12:48,720 --> 00:12:50,896
No, seriously, I'm being such a fool.

216
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:54,533
He's not so good at hiding his emotions.

217
00:13:00,060 --> 00:13:03,657
Everyone we found Dalton over here

218
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:08,600
what yeah fantastic we're coming.

219
00:13:10,720 --> 00:13:12,340
Who's Dalton?

220
00:13:16,820 --> 00:13:21,820
This is horrible I can't feel a heartbeat.

221
00:13:29,380 --> 00:13:31,145
This castle is really strange.

222
00:13:31,380 --> 00:13:33,439
It's freezing and filled with snow.

223
00:13:36,780 --> 00:13:37,997
It's cold in here!

224
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:41,198
Not the sharpest knife in
the drawer, are you, Luffy?

225
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:46,980
Look at this.

226
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:55,520
There's snow everywhere.

227
00:13:58,220 --> 00:13:59,217
And look.

228
00:13:59,300 --> 00:14:02,476
All the doors to the unused
rooms are frozen shut too.

229
00:14:17,340 --> 00:14:20,100
Come back here in just a moment, boys!

230
00:14:24,220 --> 00:14:25,977
I said come back here!

231
00:14:26,060 --> 00:14:29,137
You should rethink this idea about
asking the old hag to join our team.

232
00:14:29,220 --> 00:14:31,277
A real doctor doesn't
chase her patients around

233
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:34,184
a freaky snow-filled
castle trying to kill them!

234
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:39,500
Is it true that you guys are pirates? Yes.

235
00:14:40,700 --> 00:14:41,530
Really?

236
00:14:41,613 --> 00:14:43,320
Real pirates? Real pirates.

237
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:45,437
So you have a flag with a skull on it?

238
00:14:45,520 --> 00:14:46,350
We do.

239
00:14:46,433 --> 00:14:47,263
It's on our ship.

240
00:14:47,346 --> 00:14:49,177
So you're really
interested in pirates, huh?

241
00:14:49,260 --> 00:14:51,240
No! Not at all! You idiot!

242
00:14:52,260 --> 00:14:53,120
Shut up!

243
00:14:54,840 --> 00:14:56,437
All right, all right, I get it.

244
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:57,350
Now calm down.

245
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:00,900
But one more thing.

246
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:03,567
Do you want to come with us?

247
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:07,447
You could come sail with
us out on the ocean.

248
00:15:07,680 --> 00:15:08,510
Hmm?

249
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:10,757
If you did, that would
really help me out a lot.

250
00:15:10,840 --> 00:15:13,437
If we had a doctor on this ship, then
I wouldn't have to stay in this place?

251
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:14,597
three more days, right?

252
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:16,557
I think you'd have a really
good time if you came.

253
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:17,940
No! That's crazy!

254
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:19,788
You realize I'm a reindeer!

255
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:22,744
I don't belong on a ship
with a bunch of humans!

256
00:15:24,640 --> 00:15:26,360
I mean, just look at me.

257
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:30,317
I'm a reindeer, but I walk on two
lakes, and I talk and everything.

258
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:32,977
Animals aren't supposed to
be able to do that stuff.

259
00:15:33,060 --> 00:15:34,520
Uh, I know.

260
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:37,955
But if you're trying to scare
me off, it isn't working.

261
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:40,620
But I have a blue nose.

262
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:52,100
There you are, meat!

263
00:15:52,420 --> 00:15:53,660
Come here, Peter!

264
00:15:55,340 --> 00:15:56,380
Come back!

265
00:16:01,780 --> 00:16:03,956
Those brats sure can run, can't they?

266
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:09,360
I don't much like what you
were doing there, girl. Hmm?

267
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:13,397
Trying to tempt my reindeer away
from me without my permission.

268
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:14,310
What?

269
00:16:14,393 --> 00:16:17,786
I need your permission to make
a move on a man all of a sudden?

270
00:16:18,460 --> 00:16:19,937
No, I suppose you don't.

271
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:22,137
If you want to take him
away from here, go ahead.

272
00:16:22,220 --> 00:16:25,337
But I must warn you, it won't
be as easy as you think.

273
00:16:25,420 --> 00:16:29,361
Chopper has a scar on his heart,
a deep one my medicine can't cure.

274
00:16:29,700 --> 00:16:31,347
From the moment he was born,

275
00:16:31,560 --> 00:16:35,031
everyone, including his parents,
turned their backs on him.

276
00:16:36,440 --> 00:16:38,837
All because he was born with a blue nose.

277
00:16:38,920 --> 00:16:41,297
He was forced to walk at
the back of the group,

278
00:16:41,380 --> 00:16:43,317
separated from the rest of the reindeer,

279
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:45,929
even though he was just
a helpless newborn.

280
00:16:46,540 --> 00:16:48,680
Then one day he ate a Devil Fruit,

281
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:52,447
and he became even more of an
outcast than he had been before.

282
00:17:04,620 --> 00:17:07,417
The other reindeer pressured
him to leave the herd.

283
00:17:07,500 --> 00:17:09,477
His blue nose already made him different,

284
00:17:09,560 --> 00:17:12,619
but now he wasn't like the
ordinary reindeer at all.

285
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:15,537
Still, he was lonely and wanted friends,

286
00:17:15,620 --> 00:17:19,326
so he went down to a village
walking on two legs, as humans do.

287
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:22,497
Hey, what is that creature over there?

288
00:17:22,580 --> 00:17:26,698
But even walking on two legs, he
didn't look anything like the humans.

289
00:17:26,820 --> 00:17:30,040
And for some reason, his
nose was still blue as well.

290
00:17:30,260 --> 00:17:31,495
It looks like a Yeti!

291
00:17:31,640 --> 00:17:33,017
It's dangerous, I'm sure!

292
00:17:33,100 --> 00:17:35,041
Get the children inside, quickly!

293
00:17:36,420 --> 00:17:37,260
A gun!

294
00:17:37,500 --> 00:17:38,377
Bring me a gun!

295
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:39,457
Yeah, shoot him!

296
00:17:39,540 --> 00:17:42,540
Quick, before he runs
away! Get him! Shoot him!

297
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:44,640
Yeah, I got him!

298
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:01,237
He didn't know what was wrong.

299
00:18:01,320 --> 00:18:03,077
He couldn't understand why they reacted to

300
00:18:03,160 --> 00:18:05,497
his appearance with so
much fear and anger.

301
00:18:05,580 --> 00:18:07,080
Stay away, monster!

302
00:18:09,600 --> 00:18:11,597
He'd gone to the village seeking friends,

303
00:18:11,680 --> 00:18:13,977
but they called him a
monster and drove him away.

304
00:18:14,060 --> 00:18:17,472
He was no longer a reindeer,
but he wasn't a human either.

305
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:19,287
He was something in between.

306
00:18:20,020 --> 00:18:21,961
And so he lived alone after that,

307
00:18:22,220 --> 00:18:25,220
caught between two worlds
that wouldn't accept him.

308
00:18:25,580 --> 00:18:30,345
Now that you've heard his story, do you
think you can heal the scar on his heart?

309
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:34,337
Luffy, check out the door
at the front entrance.

310
00:18:34,420 --> 00:18:35,940
It's wide open. Huh?

311
00:18:39,860 --> 00:18:41,980
No wonder it's so cold in here.

312
00:18:42,540 --> 00:18:43,977
Anyway, let's close it.

313
00:18:44,060 --> 00:18:45,297
With it open like that,

314
00:18:45,380 --> 00:18:47,837
there's not much difference between
inside and outside the castle.

315
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:48,780
Hey, stop it!

316
00:18:48,980 --> 00:18:50,862
Don't touch that door, get away!

317
00:18:53,020 --> 00:18:54,757
Never mind him, let's close it.

318
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:56,337
Or we're gonna freeze to death.

319
00:18:56,420 --> 00:18:57,417
That's a good point.

320
00:18:57,500 --> 00:18:58,330
Stop!

321
00:18:58,413 --> 00:19:00,045
Did you guys hear what I said?

322
00:19:00,400 --> 00:19:01,260
Get back!

323
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:08,380
What is with this guy?

324
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:10,659
What the hell is he so angry about?

325
00:19:12,380 --> 00:19:14,320
Hey, come over here a second.

326
00:19:15,720 --> 00:19:16,550
Huh?

327
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:22,600
Look up there.

328
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:33,344
It's a bunch of baby snowbirds.

329
00:19:33,560 --> 00:19:35,913
See, if we closed the door, they'd fall.

330
00:19:36,120 --> 00:19:38,767
So that's the reason
they're leaving it open.

331
00:19:50,120 --> 00:19:51,100
It's freezing!

332
00:19:53,920 --> 00:19:55,820
Hold up a sec. Yeah?

333
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:58,437
That weird reindeer guy.

334
00:19:58,520 --> 00:19:59,817
Wasn't he speaking earlier?

335
00:19:59,900 --> 00:20:03,724
Now that you mention it, I remember
him walking on two legs, too.

336
00:20:04,580 --> 00:20:05,820
He's a monster!

337
00:20:08,620 --> 00:20:10,657
Okay, let's get this straight?

338
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:12,817
He walks upright and talks.

339
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:13,977
But not human.

340
00:20:14,060 --> 00:20:15,837
Has fur. He's little.

341
00:20:15,920 --> 00:20:17,137
And becomes big.

342
00:20:17,220 --> 00:20:19,200
Clearly a monster.

343
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:35,457
What a cool guy.

344
00:20:35,540 --> 00:20:36,957
I bet he's really interesting.

345
00:20:37,040 --> 00:20:38,077
hey, wait!

346
00:20:38,160 --> 00:20:40,880
I know he should join us!

347
00:21:05,540 --> 00:21:10,600
I'll do anything as
long as you are with me.

348
00:21:11,320 --> 00:21:15,860
I've grown stronger having you by my side.

349
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:20,960
We've started on an everlasting ride.

350
00:21:21,560 --> 00:21:26,257
I'm invincible when your love is near.

351
00:21:26,340 --> 00:21:31,117
When I'm with you I have no fear.

352
00:21:31,200 --> 00:21:37,577
Let's see how far we can make this go!

353
00:21:37,660 --> 00:21:40,837
The world is ours.

354
00:21:40,920 --> 00:21:42,837
You're just right, I know!

355
00:21:42,920 --> 00:21:45,597
I see it shine.

356
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:49,257
In the distance, glistening like water.

357
00:21:49,340 --> 00:21:53,340
When the sun rises in the dark.
